\section*{Reproducibility Protocol}
\label{sec:reproducibility}

This protocol defines the required datasets, solver configurations,
hardware specifications, and validation criteria necessary to reproduce
the Aether-Core/200LY simulation results, including the detection of the
3.55 keV spectral anomaly.

\subsection*{1. Required Datasets}
The following observational datasets must be used without modification:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Gaia DR3 stellar catalog (positions, velocities, magnitudes)
    \item TESS photometric variability data
    \item Derived density and kinematic fields generated from Gaia DR3
\end{itemize}

All datasets must be stored in HDF5 or Zarr format with identical
hierarchical structure.

\subsection*{2. Simulation Domain}
The simulation volume must be defined as:
\[
\Omega = [-200, 200]^3 \; \text{LY},
\]
with uniform discretization:
\[
N_x = N_y = N_z = 1024.
\]

\subsection*{3. Solver Configuration}
\subsubsection*{N-Body Gravitation}
Use a Barnes–Hut octree with opening angle:
\[
\theta = 0.7,
\]
and gravitational softening length:
\[
\epsilon = 0.01 \; \text{LY}.
\]

\subsubsection*{Magnetohydrodynamics}
Ideal MHD must be solved using:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Second-order Godunov scheme
    \item HLLD Riemann solver
    \item Hyperbolic divergence cleaning
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{4. Surrogate PINO Model}
The surrogate model must be trained using:
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{L} =
\lambda_{\text{data}} \|u - \hat{u}\|^2
+ \lambda_{\text{phys}} \|\mathcal{N}(u)\|^2,
\end{equation}
with the constraint:
\[
\text{NRMSE} < 0.05.
\]

\subsection*{5. Hardware Requirements}
The simulation must be executed on a distributed multi-GPU cluster with:
\begin{itemize}
    \item CUDA-enabled GPUs
    \item GPUDirect MPI for halo exchanges
    \item Minimum 256 GB system memory per node
\end{itemize}

Hardware differences are permitted but must be documented.

\subsection*{6. Performance Constraints}
The following constraints must be satisfied:
\begin{equation}
\frac{\Delta E}{E} < 10^{-6},
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
\frac{T_{\text{comm}}}{T_{\text{total}}} < 0.12,
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
t_{\text{step}} \le 0.15 \text{ s}.
\end{equation}

\subsection*{7. Chaos Injection Events}
To validate anomaly persistence, the following events must be introduced:
\begin{itemize}
    \item GPU memory pressure spike at iteration 250
    \item MPI jitter at iteration 600
\end{itemize}

The anomaly must remain detectable under both conditions.

\subsection*{8. Anomaly Detection Procedure}
Spectral intensity must be computed and compared to a decayed-field model:
\begin{equation}
\Delta I(E) = I_{\text{obs}}(E) - I_{\text{dec}}(E).
\end{equation}

A peak at:
\[
E = 3.55 \text{ keV}
\]
must satisfy:
\[
\frac{d\Delta I}{dE} = 0, \quad
\frac{d^2\Delta I}{dE^2} < 0.
\]

Spatial localization must yield:
\[
(120, -45, 80) \text{ LY}.
\]

\subsection*{9. Versioning and Documentation}
All reproduction attempts must include:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Code commit hash
    \item Dataset version identifiers
    \item Hardware profile
    \item Solver configuration file
\end{itemize}

